        "title": "CVE-2025-12735",
        "descriptions": [
          {
            "lang": "en",
            "value": "The expr-eval library is a JavaScript expression parser and evaluator designed to safely evaluate mathematical expressions with user-defined variables. However, due to insufficient input validation, an attacker can pass a crafted variables object into the evaluate() function and trigger arbitrary code execution."
          }
        ],
        "source": {
