      "notes": [
        {
          "category": "summary",
          "text": "An update for ruby is now available for Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9.2 Extended Update Support.\n\nRed Hat Product Security has rated this update as having a security impact of Moderate. A Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) base score, which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVE link(s) in the References section.",
          "title": "Topic"
        },
        {
          "category": "general",
          "text": "Ruby is an extensible, interpreted, object-oriented, scripting language. It has features to process text files and to perform system management tasks.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* ruby/cgi-gem: HTTP response splitting in CGI (CVE-2021-33621)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
          "title": "Details"
        },
        {
