            "category": "description",
            "text": "A flaw was found in Rubygem RDoc. When parsing .rdoc_options used for configuration in RDoc as a YAML file there are no restrictions on the classes that can be restored. This issue may lead to object injection, resulting in remote code execution.",
            "title": "Vulnerability description"
          },
          {
            "category": "summary",
            "text": "ruby: RCE vulnerability with .rdoc_options in RDoc",
            "title": "Vulnerability summary"
          },
          {
            "category": "other",
            "text": "An attacker would need to provide a maliciously crafted configuration file or documentation cache to a user in order to trigger this vulnerability.",
